Hestia: Hey Aelius, welcome in!
Hestia: It’s been over a week, how are you feeling about being here still?

-> I've enjoyed it so far. (deference)
    Hestia: That’s good to hear, I’m glad you’ve come to enjoy somewhere that isn’t home.
-> I’ve had a whimsical time here. I like it! (humorous)
    Hestia: Whimsy? I wouldn’t describe Olympus as whimsical, but if that’s a good thing, I’m glad to hear it.
-> It’s been the absolute best! (aggressive)
    Hestia: Quite the enthusiasm! Glad to see that you’re having a great time so far!

Aelius: [Positive] Of course, it’s been a wonderful time helping you out Hestia.
Aelius: [Positive] I wouldn’t trade the experience for anything. I just wish I could maybe talk to my mom…
Hestia: I appreciate that, Aelius. Also, you’ll be pleased to hear: Hades sent a messenger last night to me. He mentioned that a meeting with your mother has been set up for tomorrow.
Aelius: [Positive] Wait, what- I’ll finally get to see her?!
Hestia: Yes dear, you’ll get to see your mother shortly.
Aelius: [Positive] Thank you, Hestia, thank you so much!
Hestia: Don’t thank just me. It seems that a lot of the Olympians also sent word to Hades asking for the same thing.
Aelius: [Positive] I- I have no words. I’m so thankful to everyone for how kind they’ve been to me while I’ve been here.
Hestia: It was only fair, in just the short time you’ve been helping me, you’ve been able to solve a great many of the issues that we’ve had here.
Hestia: Ares and Hephaestus can tolerate each other at the moment. Zeus is making an effort to be part of the family. Hermes is opening up.
Hestia: Despite these issues persisting as long as I can remember, you’ve come in and changed us for the better.
Aelius: [Positive] Well, I think just having a different perspective can be all the difference.
Aelius: It’s only been the same people here forever, so of course nothing really changes, even if you try.
Hestia: Either way, thank you. From all of us.
Aelius: No, thank you. You’ve taken me to my family and shown me the rest of the family I never knew.

// DING MF

Hestia: As grateful for having you here as I am, it seems we have a guest.
Hestia: If you could go get their order, that would be most appreciated.
Aelius: [Positive] Of course! I’ll talk to you in a bit, then!
